From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 03:57:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: apple: t8132: Describe the nub SPMI controller's
 interrupt

The nub SPMI controller (nub-spmi0, the bus of the main PMU) raises AIC
interrupt 513 and is the interrupt controller of its peripherals, as
nub-spmi-a0 is with AIC 520. Describe both, so that a peripheral
interrupt such as the PMU's RTC alarm can be requested.

Values from the ADT, not copied from another board:
- J604 boot ADT (MEASURED, 2026-11-04 first-boot capture, sha256
  e7af8fd7...) and the j604ap 25G83 and 26B123 templates (SOURCE):
  /arm-io/nub-spmi0 has interrupt-parent = <self aic self> and
  interrupts = <256 513 ...>; the first entry after 256 is the AIC
  line. The same layout on /arm-io/nub-spmi-a0 gives 520, which is the
  value this file already uses for nub_spmi_a0.
- The j713ap templates have the same 513, so this is a SoC property.

With an interrupt the driver waits for the RX FIFO on the notify
interrupt instead of polling it, as on nub-spmi-a0.

Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5.5
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132.dtsi | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132.dtsi
index 2ae3200ebe..7eb1ecb1d9 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132.dtsi
@@ -748,6 +748,10 @@
 			reg = <0x3 0x88714000 0x0 0x100>;
 			#address-cells = <2>;
 			#size-cells = <0>;
+			#interrupt-cells = <2>;
+			interrupt-controller;
+			interrupt-parent = <&aic>;
+			interrupts = <AIC_IRQ 513 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>;
 			power-domains = <&ps_nub_spmi0>;
 			status = "disabled";
 		};
